“Neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I am a dry tree.
For thus saith the Lord unto the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose the things that please me, and take hold of my covenant;
Even unto them will I give in mine house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters…”

This is the difference between Nabal and the redeemed:
one hardens his heart and dies in his sin;
the other bows before Jesus and lives by mercy.

Comparison doesn’t always shout.
Sometimes it whispers in quiet moments—
while you scroll,
while you pray,
while you wait.

“Wait for the Lord;
be strong, and let your heart take courage;
wait for the Lord!” — Book of Psalms 27:14

“His snorting throws out flashes of light…
flames stream from his mouth;
sparks of fire shoot out.” — Job 41:18–19 (NIV)

“For the vision is yet for an appointed time;
but at the end it shall speak, and not lie:
though it tarry, wait for it;
because it will surely come, it will not tarry.”
— KJV
